2. **Case-sensitivity vs. tests:** `Cp05Tests` requires case-insensitive duplicate detection (upper/lower-cased last name + same telephone must return 409). The current `isSameIdentity` uses case-sensitive `Objects.equals` on `lastName`, and `findByLastName` is almost certainly a case-sensitive lookup — so `Cp05Tests` would not pass with the present logic. This appears to be the "name uniqueness" gap referenced by the recent commits. (Reported for awareness only; no changes made.)

